[], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2980594275772775, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07573790368182498, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81680965, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eea7a8d68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 834, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:45\", \"token_count\": 328, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \" - *Refactoring stream buffer release after each chunk after the task was reopened when files 2GB and larger were still found to leak memory.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"refactor stream buffer releas after each chunk after the task wa reopen when file 2gb and larger were still found to leak memori\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee5a9c8a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"id\": \"c9b7e08e10c6b0f5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23986246123144742, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.02163940175921063, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7490496, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee5a9c8a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1122, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:55\", \"token_count\": 577, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd stream chunking so large, multi-GB PDF documents can be processed without excessive memory pressure. Chunking was merged, but the task was reopened after files over 2GB were found to still leak memory; buffer-release logic is being refactored to release buffers after each chunk.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Large PDF documents are processed via stream chunking rather than loading whole files into memory.\\n\\n- Memory buffers are released after each chunk, with no leak on files 2GB and larger.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd stream chunking so large, multi-GB PDF documents can be processed without excessive memory pressure. Chunking was merged, but the task was reopened after files over 2GB were found to still leak memory; buffer-release logic is being refactored to release buffers after each chunk.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-12**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because large-file chunking is needed for multi-GB documents.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-20**: Charlie - Buffer Release Refactor (Active (Reopened))\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 descript add stream chunk so larg multi gb pdf document can be process without excess memori pressur chunk wa merg but the task wa reopen after file over 2gb were found to still leak memori buffer releas logic is be refactor to releas buffer after each chunk clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 accept criterion larg pdf document are process via stream chunk rather than load whole file into memori memori buffer are releas after each chunk with no leak on file 2gb and larger clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 descript add stream chunk so larg multi gb pdf document can be process without excess memori pressur chunk wa merg but the task wa reopen after file over 2gb were found to still leak memori buffer releas logic is be refactor to releas buffer after each chunk clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 activ histori 2026 08 12 alic task creat open open the task becaus larg file chunk is need for multi gb document 2026 08 20 charli buffer releas refactor activ reopen\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee5a9c8a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"id\": \"dfbb498e251867d1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23895661123144743, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.02163940175921063, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7460301, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee5a9c8a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1122, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:55\", \"token_count\": 577, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nBob reported offline-auth rotation cannot complete without network access — left blocked. Evan's disk-usage monitor loop is in; Diana's halt-behavior sign-off still pending.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Bob**: Offline-auth mock first — not well. I built the local mock and ran the rotation flow with the network denied. Rotation can't complete offline.\\n\\n**Diana**: Is that a bug in the mock, or the design?\\n\\n**Bob**: The design. The flow we picked assumes a connection to finish rotation. I don't have a fix yet — we should call it blocked.\\n\\n**Alice**: Agreed. Offline auth stays blocked until we have an offline-capable rotation approach. Evan, status on the disk-usage monitor?\\n\\n**Evan**: Monitor loop is in. It watches disk usage so we can enforce the quota policy. Haven't had Diana sign off on the halt behavior yet.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Has anyone verified the halt behavior yet?\\n\\n**Evan**: Not signed off. Monitor is in progress; Diana still needs to confirm it actually stops writes at the configured quota.\\n\\n**Evan**: I'll wait on Diana's halt sign-off before calling quota monitoring done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari bob report offlin auth rotat can not complet without network access left block evan s disk usag monitor loop is in diana s halt behavior sign off still pend sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript bob offlin auth mock first not well i built the local mock and ran the rotat flow with the network deni rotat can t complet offlin diana is that a bug in the mock or the design bob the design the flow we pick assum a connect to finish rotat i don t have a fix yet we should call it block alic agre offlin auth stay block until we have an offlin capabl rotat approach evan status on the disk usag monitor evan monitor loop is in it watch disk usag so we can enforc the quota polici haven t had diana sign off on the halt behavior yet charli ha anyon verifi the halt behavior yet evan not sign off monitor is in progress diana still need to confirm it actual stop write at the configur quota evan i ll wait on diana s halt sign off befor call quota monitor done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee33c45c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"bdd05a8ed6c9e627\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2379938872570021, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.036065668938574456, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70915973, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee33c45c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1273, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:29\", \"token_count\": 368, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"7d969f7c78a9200e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2367648397442248, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.028852535348892542, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72189355, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:23\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"CIPH-32 storage quota management marked done hard-halt check later evidence reopened monitor 500MB buffer tolerance\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"As of 2026-09-22, T022 / CIPH-32 is **reopened and active**; verification of the quota-monitor buffer refactor remains pending. *(WS-07, S4)*\n\nIt was reopened on 2026-09-15 after production-like batches hit the **500 MB hard halt before doing useful work**—showing the flat cutoff was too aggressive. *(SRC-SLACK-23)*\n\nThe monitor is being changed from that hard 500 MB cutoff to a **10% buffer tolerance above quota**. Production planning also sets the free-disk baseline at **2 GB, not 500 MB**. Bob refactored the loop; a September 18 retest reported no premature halts, with final refactor verification still needed. *(WS-07; SRC-SLACK-23; SRC-CU-CIPH-32)*"}}
